│   Message:                                                                                                                                     │
│     I fixed two ZWJ/variation-selector edge cases in `rich/cells.py`, and submitted the patch (1 file changed). The issue text was terse, so I │
│ inferred the bugs from the code rather than from a specific spec. The fix targets the crash and hang I could reproduce, and the existing       │
│ `tests/test_cells.py` suite still passes (54 tests).                                                                                           │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     - **Trailing ZWJ crash:** `_cell_len` called `next()` on the iterator after a zero-width joiner, which raised `StopIteration` when the     │
│ joiner was the last character. It now uses `next(iter_characters, None)`.                                                                      │
│     - **Leading variation selector hang:** `split_graphemes` only advanced its index for a variation selector when a previous character had    │
│ been measured. A leading `\ufe0f` left the index unchanged and looped forever. The selector branch now always advances, and the ZWJ span end   │
│ is clamped to the string length.                                                                                                               │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     I checked these by hand: `cell_len('a\u200d')` returns 1, `split_graphemes('\ufe0f')` returns `([], 0)`, and `\u2764\ufe0f` still measures │
│ 2 cells. I did not check the patch against the hidden tests for issues #3947 and #3950, since I don't have their exact expectations.           │
